/// <summary>
/// A configurable, disk-backed batch iterator over a standard image dataset.
/// </summary>
/// <remarks>
/// <para>Datasets: "mnist" and "fashion_mnist" (28x28 grayscale, 10 classes; 60000 train / 10000
/// test), "cifar10" (32x32 RGB, 10 classes; 50000 / 10000) and "cifar100" (32x32 RGB, 100 fine
/// or 20 coarse classes; 50000 / 10000).</para>
/// <para>Iteration works in epochs. has_next()/next() walk the current epoch's order; reset() starts
/// the next epoch (with a fresh shuffle when shuffling is on). Every setter returns the loader
/// for chaining and rewinds the current epoch, so configure before iterating.</para>
/// <para>Reading is const and opens files per call, so batch()/take() may be called from several
/// threads at once; next()/reset() and the setters mutate and must not race.</para>
/// <para><b>Example</b></para>
/// <code>
/// dm::datasets::ImageLoader test("cifar10", "test");
/// test.set_batch_size(500).set_layout("nchw").set_normalize(false);
/// const auto first = test.next();          // shape {500, 3, 32, 32}, values 0..255
/// std::print("{}\n", test.class_names()[first.labels[0]]);   // "cat"
/// </code>
/// </remarks>
