    /// <summary>
    /// Builds a frequency histogram of <c>data</c> with <c>bins</c> equal-width bins, like R's
    /// <c>hist(x, breaks = bins)</c>.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// <para>The bins split [min, max] of the data into equal widths (R instead treats <c>breaks</c> as a
    /// suggestion and uses <c>pretty()</c> boundaries). Bins include their left edge and exclude their
    /// right edge, except that the maximum goes in the final bin; R's default (<c>right = TRUE</c>) is
    /// the opposite, so a value on an inner boundary is counted one bin higher here. Constant
    /// data uses the range [value, value + 1]. Each bin is one bar of height equal to its count,
    /// centered on the bin with width equal to the bin width. The title is "Histogram", the x
    /// label "x", and the y label "Frequency". The data is consumed; the plot keeps only counts.</para>
