    /// <summary>
    /// Builds side-by-side box-and-whisker plots, one per group, like R's
    /// <c>boxplot(list(...), names = names)</c>.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// <para>Group g is drawn at x = g (0, 1, 2, ...) as a 0.6-unit-wide box from the first to the
    /// third quartile with a line at the median. Quartiles are R's default "type 7" sample
    /// quantiles. Whiskers reach the most extreme values within 1.5 IQR of the box (Tukey's
    /// rule), and values beyond are drawn as outlier points. R's <c>boxplot()</c> instead uses
    /// Tukey's hinges (<c>fivenum()</c>), so for some sample sizes the box edges and the fences differ
    /// slightly from R: for 1, ..., 9, 40 this gives quartiles 3.25 and 7.75 where R draws
    /// hinges at 3 and 8. All boxes share <c>color</c>; the title and axis labels keep their defaults.</para>
    /// <para><b>Example</b></para>
    /// <code>
    /// auto plt = dm::Plot::boxplot({{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 40}, {2, 4, 6}}, {"a", "b"});
    /// const auto&amp; y = plt.series()[0].y;  // whisker_lo, q1, median, q3, whisker_hi, outliers...
    /// std::print("{} {} {} {} {} | {}\n", y[0], y[1], y[2], y[3], y[4], y[5]);
    /// // 1 3.25 5.5 7.75 9 | 40
    /// plt.save("boxes.svg");
    /// </code>
    /// <para><b>References</b></para>
    /// <para>- J. W. Tukey (1977). Exploratory Data Analysis. Addison-Wesley. (Box plot and the 1.5 IQR fences.)
    /// - R. McGill, J. W. Tukey, W. A. Larsen (1978). "Variations of Box Plots". The American
    ///   Statistician 32(1), 12-16. doi:10.1080/00031305.1978.10479236
    /// - R. J. Hyndman, Y. Fan (1996). "Sample Quantiles in Statistical Packages". The American
    ///   Statistician 50(4), 361-365. doi:10.1080/00031305.1996.10473566 (quantile type 7.)
    /// - R <c>boxplot()</c>: https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/boxplot.html
    /// - R <c>boxplot.stats()</c>: https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/grDevices/html/boxplot.stats.html</para>
    /// <para>See also: <c>box()</c>, <c>x_tick_labels()</c>.</para>
    /// <para>Uses the C++ default for <c>names = default</c>, <c>color</c>.</para>
    /// </remarks>
