    /// <c>\Delta H=r^2f(\phi)</c> with <c>f=\tfrac12(|M^L(\cos\phi,\sin\phi)|^2-1)</c>, and because
    /// <c>r^2/2\sim\text{Exp}(1)</c> the radial average of <c>\min(1,e^{-\Delta H})</c> is
    /// <c>1/(1+2f)</c> for <c>f&gt;0</c> and 1 otherwise. The angle is integrated numerically.</para>
