    public static HypothesisTestResult FTestVariance(IEnumerable<double> x, IEnumerable<double> y, Alternative alternative, double confLevel) => Rosetta.To<HypothesisTestResult>(Rosetta.Call(204, x, y, alternative, confLevel));

    /// <summary>
    /// Normal-approximation Wilcoxon signed-rank test with tie/continuity corrections.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// <para>Tests symmetry of x-mu about zero under independent observations, not an arbitrary-population
    /// mean or median null. For paired data pass aligned differences. Exact-zero differences are
    /// removed; absolute differences receive average ranks. Always uses a normal approximation, even
    /// for small tie-free samples; no exact option or CI. O(n log n) work/O(n) storage; input
    /// unchanged, no shared state.</para>
    /// <para><b>Example</b></para>
    /// <code>
    /// const auto w=dm::stats::wilcoxon_signed_rank_test({1,2,3,4});
    /// std::print("{:.0f}\n",w.statistic); // 10
    /// </code>
    /// <para><b>References</b></para>
    /// <para>- https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/wilcox.test.html</para>
    /// <para>See also: <c>HypothesisTestResult</c>.</para>
    /// <para>Uses the C++ default for <c>mu = 0.0</c>, <c>alternative = Alternative.TwoSided</c>.</para>
    /// </remarks>
    /// <param name="x">Finite values; at least one nonzero difference from mu must remain.</param>
    /// <returns>statistic=positive rank sum V, estimate1=mu (not an estimated pseudomedian), approximate p_value; no CI.</returns>
    /// <exception cref="NativeException">C++ <c>std::invalid_argument</c>: Nonfinite input/mu, invalid alternative, no nonzero differences or zero rank variance.</exception>
    public static HypothesisTestResult WilcoxonSignedRankTest(IEnumerable<double> x) => Rosetta.To<HypothesisTestResult>(Rosetta.Call(205, x));

    /// <summary>
    /// Normal-approximation Wilcoxon signed-rank test with tie/continuity corrections.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// <para>Tests symmetry of x-mu about zero under independent observations, not an arbitrary-population
    /// mean or median null. For paired data pass aligned differences. Exact-zero differences are
    /// removed; absolute differences receive average ranks. Always uses a normal approximation, even
    /// for small tie-free samples; no exact option or CI. O(n log n) work/O(n) storage; input
    /// unchanged, no shared state.</para>
    /// <para><b>Example</b></para>
    /// <code>
    /// const auto w=dm::stats::wilcoxon_signed_rank_test({1,2,3,4});
    /// std::print("{:.0f}\n",w.statistic); // 10
    /// </code>
    /// <para><b>References</b></para>
    /// <para>- https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/wilcox.test.html</para>
    /// <para>See also: <c>HypothesisTestResult</c>.</para>
    /// <para>Uses the C++ default for <c>alternative = Alternative.TwoSided</c>.</para>
    /// </remarks>
    /// <param name="x">Finite values; at least one nonzero difference from mu must remain.</param>
